what color is cyborg blood supposed to  be how many bodies does elita actually  have what exactly are those blue flames  keep watching for the elita battle angel  details only real fans notice  one of the most memorable and exciting  parts of elita battle angel is the high  octane spectacle that is motorball there  are two matches in the film a skirmish  on the streets of iron city and a  professional tryout in a super-sized  stadium despite these two sequences  being decidedly different in terms of  the tone stakes and even the visual  presentation both of them utilize  real-world camera physics even though  the limitations of real-world cameras  don't apply when creating an action  scene with cgi director robert rodriguez  chose to self-impose those limitations  to create a more grounded sequence in an  interview with inverse he described his  methodology for crafting the scene with  a sense of realism as he revealed i  don't want the cameras flying around the  place doing things impossible to shoot i  wanted the physics of real cameras  placement you would see in nascar long  lenses capturing things whizzing by as  well as cameras on the track with the  players to keep it as real world as  possible pulling inspiration from the  shooting style of real world sports and  sticking only to shots that would be  possible with a physical camera  ultimately grounded the bombastic action  with a sense of reality  the character of elita starts out the  film as a total amnesiac while  struggling to recall details from her  past she finds herself stumbling into  some dangerous situations luckily she  possesses an instinctive fighting  technique that kicks in when she's  threatened this combat style is known as  panzer kunst a german term which  translates into english as armor art  panzer kunst comes directly from the  manga series that inspired the film  within the series lore panzer kunst  originated on mars as a martial art  style for use in zero gravity combat in  real life panzerkunst refers to the art  of defeating armored opponents in combat  which is fitting considering that the  majority of combatants in elita are  heavily armored cyborgs the first  descriptions of real-life panzerkunst in  sword fighting are believed to come from  a german fencing manual from the 1440s  this instructional guide offered  insights into fighting techniques to be  used against both armored and unarmored  opponents in a variety of combat  situations though the manual was  primarily focused on fencing there were  also techniques described for other  weaponry and also unarmed combat azaleta  typically dispatches her foes with a  mixture of martial arts abilities and  sword-fighting prowess her fighting  style lines up well with this 15th  century inspiration  after being brought back into  consciousness for the first time in  centuries by dr ido elita is a blank  slate in her quest for self-discovery  she seeks to learn not only who she is  but also what she believes and what she  likes and dislikes when hugo learned  that elita has never tasted chocolate  before he sets about remedying that  immediately so after trying it for the  first time elita declares that she now  has a favorite food  i have a favorite food now  [Music]  this is my favorite food it might look  like a simple chocolate bar but it's  actually a chocolate shell packed with a  honey peanut butter filling and pecans  we know this because it was made by  robert rodriguez himself and he even put  together a tutorial explaining how to  make your own at home he used a 3d  printer to make a custom chocolate mold  in the shape of the zollum symbol found  in the world of elita and he even  brought homemade snacks to the cast of  the film as well throughout his career  rodriguez's love of food has popped up  in his work time and time again as  evidenced by his long-running 10-minute  cooking school series that often appears  in the dvd extras of his movies this has  included making texas barbecue for  planet terror presenting his recipe for  breakfast tacos for sin city and  explaining how to cook puerto pebil for  once upon a time in mexico  long before the elita battle angel film  arrived in theaters the story was first  told in manga form all the way back in  1990. the first run of the manga series  ran for nine volumes that were released  over the course of five years and  multiple sequel series followed in  english this manga is known as battle  angel alita though the original japanese  title translates directly as gun dream  during an interview with bbc radio 1  james cameron described the switch from  battle angel elita to elita battle angel  as a forward-thinking shift with sequels  in mind he suggested such potential  sequel titles as elita fallen angel and  elita avenging angel in the manga and in  the 1993 anime adaptation battle angel  the main character's name wasn't elita  at all but rather galley the name was  changed for the initial english  translation and it stuck around for the  big screen version as well there's  another important difference in elita's  namesake that changed between the manga  and the film in the manga dr ito names  gali after his cat who recently passed  away while the live-action adaptation  ups the ante and has dr ido named alita  after his dead daughter  there are a couple of moments in elita  battle angel when little blue flames  emerge from elita's body though never  explicitly explained in the film they  play an important role later on in the  plot and serve an even more important  purpose in the manga in the manga lore  these little flames are an extension of  alita's ability to manipulate plasma  what might look like a flame is actually  arc plasma these plasma powers  contribute to elita's fighting prowess  by increasing her speed and magnifying  the power of her strikes when she throws  a punch it isn't just a synthetic fist  striking her opponent but also the  destructive power of plasma energy  toward the end of the film when she  finally gets her hands on the much  sought after damascus blade her arc  plasma abilities come into play again  you might notice that the blade turns  blue and glows in her hand something it  never did while in zapan's possession  this is due to her arc plasma powers  surging through the blade and  supercharging it  didn't exactly come with a manual did  you elita battle angel was released in  the united states on february 14 2019  but james cameron bought the film rights  to the manga all the way back in 2000.  he even expressed interest in one day  adapting the story as early as 1995  before the release of titanic he was  ultimately able to buy the adaptation  rights directly from the manga's creator  for the sum of 1 million yen cameron  originally planned on directing the film  himself and he considered going into  production on elita instead of 2009's  avatar of course that didn't end up  happening one key reason for holding off  on alita was that he didn't think cgi  technology was quite ready to deliver  what was needed to do it properly after  the massive financial success and major  technological innovations of avatar  cameron again toyed around with the idea  of directing elita but his attachments  to the avatar sequels made that  impossible enter robert rodriguez a  friend of cameron's for many years who  had seen materials from cameron's  earlier false starts with elita he asked  if the adaptation would ever happen if  cameron was going to be busy with the  avatar franchise for the rest of his  career so cameron then offered rodriguez  the reigns as rodriguez told fandango  all access because we've been looking  for things to work with on together for  years and this was a perfect opportunity  for a collaboration  the blue blood of the cyborgs in elita  might feel reminiscent of other sci-fi  properties such as the inky blue blood  of the androids in 2013's the world's  end but the blood in elita wasn't always  blue in the 1993 anime adaptation battle  angel the cyborg blood was instead a  bright crimson and although the manga  was inked in black and white there was a  clear emphasis on gore that didn't make  it into the 2019 film in an interview  with bbc radio 1 james cameron revealed  that he couldn't be completely faithful  to the manga because of how gory it was  so they softened it for a pg-13 rating  even with this softening elita pushes  the limits of pg-13 as there's plenty of  biomechanical destruction and  dismemberment the mpaa's ratings board  has historically been more lenient when  assigning ratings to films with  unnaturally colored blood so tinting the  cyborg blood blue helped to avoid an r  rating this isn't the first film  directed by robert rodriguez to use  unnaturally colored blood in a bid to  procure a more audience friendly rating  as 1996's from dusk till dawn featured  green blood for the vampires instead of  red that decision was made out of a fear  of receiving an nc-17 which worked out  in the film's favor as it ultimately  secured an r rating alita gets her first  taste of motorball while playing in a  friendly neighborhood skirmish in  contrast to the later stadium motorball  match this first game was intended to be  executed with little to no cgi outside  of the title character this requirement  incurred a number of additional  challenges the first of which was  finding the right talent to fill the  roles of the other players who had to  play this larger-than-life sport as if  it was second nature so stunt  coordinator garrett warren brought  together the world's top professional  inline skaters to execute the scene in a  making of video warren producer john  landau and members of the cast and stunt  team discuss how the unique challenges  of the scene were overcome tall drop-in  ramps and mechanical winches were used  to mimic the speed and momentum achieved  by the motorized rollerblades of the  film which don't exist in real life  the special effects of elita battle  angel exist at the cutting edge of  what's possible with modern filmmaking  technology having a large budget wasn't  all that it took to pull off the  impressive visuals as it also required  the best design team and technology  available rather than scouring the  industry for the best in the business  the necessary resources came from a  little closer to home james cameron had  already assembled the perfect design  team to work on the avatar sequels so  when robert rodriguez got started on  elita cameron lent him the team for a  few months to work out the look feel and  creation of the characters and world the  production also made use of the motion  capture and 3d camera technologies  previously pioneered by cameron for both  the avatar sequels and his documentary  projects cameron wanted a realistic nuts  and bolts look to the cyborgs and the  world while rodriguez pulled from his  experiences as a cartoonist to bring a  lighter sense of style to the film's  look and feel ultimately a happy medium  was found with this design team  the only human part of elita's  physiology is her brain while the rest  of her body is synthetic even her heart  is a pricey centuries-old relic this  means that her body can be swapped out  with different cyborg parts tailored to  specific tasks in the film we see her in  two main cyborg bodies one is a civilian  body initially built in part for dr  ido's daughter before her death while  the other is a reclaimed berserker body  built for combat there are also a few  quick glimpses at another cyborg body in  flashbacks warrior's spirit needs a  warrior's body  however in the manga and anime alita has  even more cyborg bodies that she can  switch between that are best suited to  particular activities before the  motorball match in the film dr ito  insists that alita wear protective pads  on top of her berserker body but in the  manga lore alita has a specialized body  made just for motorball this motorball  body has less destructive capabilities  than her berserker body but it's much  faster and more flexible if elita battle  angel ever winds up getting a sequel  there's a chance we might see more of  her specialized cyborg bodies  [Applause]  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

